("US federal debt is about $39.5 trillion, near 99% of GDP and on track to break the post-war record; about $116,000 per American.","39.5 trillion in federal debt near 99%","K02: 39.5T / 342M = $115,500. Gross debt near $39T in mid-2026 and debt held by the public near 99-100% of GDP are consistent by analyst recall; the 99% applies to public debt, not the $39.5T gross figure.",[]),
("America spent about $970 billion on interest last year, the third-largest budget line, bigger than defence, about 19% of revenue and $7,300 per household.","America spent about $970","NI1: FY2025 net interest $970.4B (Treasury), about 19% of revenue and 3.2% of GDP; larger than defence. K02: 970B / 132M households = $7,350. Correct.",['NI1']),
("That is $2.8 billion a day; five years ago it was $345 billion and has nearly tripled.","that is $2.8","K02: 970 / 365 = $2.66B a day, so $2.8B is slightly high; FY2020 net interest $345B (analyst recall) gives 2.8x, \"nearly tripled\". Mostly correct.",['NI1']),
("About $9 trillion of Treasury debt matured last year, a quarter of the national debt.","about $9 trillion","K02: 9 / 38.5 = 23%. Plausible by analyst recall for coupon-and-note maturities; bills roll far more often, so the figure depends on the measure.",[]),
("Foreigners hold about 24% of US debt; Japan is the largest foreign holder; China holds under 2%, its lowest since 2008.","Foreigners hold about 24%","Consistent by analyst recall with Treasury TIC data (foreign holdings about $9T; China about $750B, about 2% of total debt). The narrator's \"24 3/4\" is a garble of \"three quarters\".",[]),
